<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>A school farm made a profit of Ksh <m>28\,000</m>. The profit is shared among the Agriculture, Environment and Science clubs in the ratio <m>3 : 5 : 6</m>. Find each share.</p><p>Agriculture club: Ksh <fillin characters="8" name="ans1"/>  </p><p>Environment club: Ksh <fillin characters="8" name="ans2"/>  </p><p>Science club: Ksh <fillin characters="8" name="ans3"/>  </p></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Find one part first, then each share is a number of parts.</p><p>Total number of parts: <m>{3} + {5} + {6} = {14}</m>.</p><p>One part: <m>{28\,000} \div {14} = {2000}</m>.</p><p>Shares: <m>{3} \times {2000} = {6000}</m>, <m>{5} \times {2000} = {10\,000}</m> and <m>{6} \times {2000} = {12\,000}</m>.</p><p>Check: <m>{6000} + {10\,000} + {12\,000} = {28\,000}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>6000</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>10000</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>12000</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>